From: Cubie A7S bringup <local>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: axp2101: register the axp2xx-watchdog cell for the AXP8191 variant


System #9 enabled CONFIG_AW_AXP_WATCHDOG=y (the one-line fix TF asked for in the
#8 receipt) and the driver is now built in -- /sys/bus/platform/drivers/
axp2xx-watchdog exists -- but the watchdog still never appears:

    $ ls /sys/class/watchdog/            -> only watchdog0   (2050000.watchdog, SoC)
    $ ls /sys/bus/platform/devices/      -> only 2050000.watchdog
    $ dmesg | grep -i axp2xx             -> nothing

Root cause: the MFD cell that instantiates the driver is defined only in
axp2101_cells[] (this file, line 2191):

        {
                .name = "axp2xx-watchdog",
                .of_compatible = "x-powers,axp2xx-watchdog",
        },

but this board reports "AXP20x variant AXP8191 found" and the variant dispatch
therefore registers axp8191_cells[] instead:

        axp2101.c:4255   axp20x->nr_cells = ARRAY_SIZE(axp8191_cells);
        axp2101.c:4256   axp20x->cells    = axp8191_cells;

axp8191_cells[] (line 3145) has no watchdog entry, so mfd_add_devices() never
creates the platform device, the driver's probe is never called, and the DTB
node (which #8/#9 already ship: twi@7083000/pmu@36/watchdog,
compatible = "x-powers,axp2xx-watchdog", status = "okay") has nothing to bind to.

Patch 0019 in the TF series added the driver, the Kconfig symbol and the
Makefile line, and explicitly did NOT add this cell because "our tree already
has it" -- true for axp2101_cells[], wrong for the array this board uses.

Fix: add the same cell to axp8191_cells[].  Nothing else changes; the driver and
its of_match_table are already correct, and the node stays optional (a DTB
without the node simply gets no watchdog device).

Expected after rebuild (system #10):

    $ ls /sys/class/watchdog/
    watchdog0  watchdog1
    $ dmesg | grep -i axp2xx
    axp2xx-watchdog 7083000.twi:pmu@36:watchdog: ... (driver banner)

Note on the acceptance criteria: CONFIG_WATCHDOG_SYSFS is not set in this
config, so /sys/class/watchdog/*/{identity,state,timeout} are not created for
ANY watchdog (the SoC one has none either).  Judge WD-2/WD-3 by the device
count plus `wdctl` / dmesg, or add CONFIG_WATCHDOG_SYSFS=y to the config
(TF has flagged this in the #9 receipt).

Baseline: bsp/drivers/power/mfd/axp2101.c:3145 (axp8191_cells[]) and :2191 (the
cell as it exists in axp2101_cells[]); verified with --fuzz=0 against the tree
Armbian actually builds.

Signed-off-by: Cubie A7S bringup <local>
---
diff --git a/bsp/drivers/power/mfd/axp2101.c b/bsp/drivers/power/mfd/axp2101.c
--- a/bsp/drivers/power/mfd/axp2101.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/power/mfd/axp2101.c
@@ -3160,6 +3160,10 @@ static struct mfd_cell axp8191_cells[] = {
 		.num_resources = ARRAY_SIZE(axp8191_temp_ctrl_resources),
 
 	},
+	{
+		.name = "axp2xx-watchdog",
+		.of_compatible = "x-powers,axp2xx-watchdog",
+	},
 	{
 		.of_compatible = "xpower-vregulator,dcdc1",
 		.name = "reg-virt-consumer",
